"""Model-facing text variants of the shipped MCP server for A/B tests (EXP-009).

Each variant overrides ``build_mcp(service, surface)``: keys ``instructions``, ``search_cards``,
``find_similar``, ``get_card``, ``list_tags``. "v1" = the text as shipped in server.py (2026-10-14).
"v3" = v2 + the EXP-007 tool-hint sentence in the instructions.
"v2" = the rewrite proposed in docs/mcp_instructions_research.md §3 (trigger in the instructions,
"even when you feel sure", self-contained descriptions, no duplicated filter/output prose).
"""

SURFACES: dict[str, dict[str, str]] = {
    "v1": {},
    "v2": {
        'instructions': 'Magic: The Gathering (MTG) card search and lookup over the full Oracle card database (Scryfall data, which can include cards printed after your training data). Use these tools whenever a task involves choosing, suggesting or checking cards: building, upgrading or cutting a Commander/EDH or other deck, "cards that do X", replacements for a card, or a card\'s exact text, rulings, colour identity or format legality. Use them even when you feel sure from memory: errata, new cards, and colour-identity or legality slips are the usual errors.\nEfficient use: one search_cards call per deck need, with color_identity (and format) set, returns candidates that are already in colour and legal; send 2-4 queries in that call for a broad need. get_card checks one card you named from memory or whose rulings matter. find_similar gives alternatives to a known card, e.g. for a swap. list_tags only helps find role vocabulary. Rankings use rules text only.',
        'search_cards': 'Search every Magic: The Gathering (MTG) card by what it does: semantic search over Oracle rules text, with filters for Commander colour identity, format legality, card type and mana value. Use it to find candidates for a deck need (removal, ramp, card draw, sacrifice outlets, answers to fliers, ...) rather than listing cards from memory. With color_identity (and format="commander") set, every result is in colour and legal, so no separate check is needed.\n\nPhrase each query the way the card itself is worded, not the way a player describes it, e.g. "Destroy target creature with flying.", "Whenever another creature you control dies, draw a card." Put colour, format, type and mana-value constraints in the filter arguments, not in the query text.\n- Narrow effect: send 1 precise query.\n- Open-ended need: send 2-4 `queries`, each a *different* mechanism, e.g. "I keep losing to fliers" -> ["Reach", "Destroy target creature with flying.", "Creatures you control gain reach until end of turn."]. Their rankings are fused.\nWrite one clean sentence per query, not a whole invented card, and don\'t add the user\'s own wording as a query.\n\nResults are ranked by text relevance only, never by how widely played a card is. Filters apply before ranking, so even narrow filters return the best matches. Default: 15 cards, compact (oracle text cut at ~250 characters per face, plus roles, legality and Game Changer markers), about 2,000 tokens. Use limit 30-50 only to survey a role; use get_card or detail="full" for complete text.',
        'find_similar': 'Find Magic: The Gathering (MTG) cards that do what a given card does: replacements, upgrades and redundancy. Use it when the user wants "more cards like X", a stand-in for a card that is off-colour or not legal in their format, or, in a swap, an in-colour alternative to the card being cut. `card_name` is fuzzy-matched; that card\'s Oracle text is the query and the card itself is excluded. Takes the same filters as search_cards, e.g. find_similar("Rhystic Study", color_identity="BR", format="commander"). Ranked by rules-text similarity only; same compact output as search_cards.',
        'get_card': 'Look up one Magic: The Gathering (MTG) card by name (fuzzy: "fire ice", "jace mind sculptor" or one face of a double-faced card all work). Returns the current Oracle text of every face, mana cost and value, type line, P/T, colours and colour identity, legality in every format, markers (Game Changer, Reserved, Commander-eligible), functional tags, official rulings and the Scryfall link. Use it before recommending or judging a card you know only from memory, and when exact wording, a ruling or legality decides the answer. About 300-1,500 tokens per card; cards found with filtered search_cards need no second check.',
        'list_tags': 'List Scryfall oracle tags: community labels for what MTG cards do (e.g. "removal", "mana-rock", "free-sacrifice-outlet", "draw-engine"), with card counts and descriptions. Use it rarely: to find the usual name for a deck role before wording a search_cards query, or to see example cards for one tag. `prefix` filters by slug prefix (falling back to substring matches); an exact slug also lists up to 15 example cards (alphabetical). The same tags appear on the `roles:` line of every search result.',
    },
}
# v3 = v2 + the one sentence that triggered tool use from the system prompt in EXP-007 (prompts.TOOL_HINT),
# moved into the server instructions: tests whether the channel (server vs system prompt) or the wording matters.
SURFACES["v3"] = {**SURFACES["v2"], "instructions": SURFACES["v2"]["instructions"] + (
    "\nBefore you answer a deck-building request, use the tools: search for candidate cards and check exact card "
    "text, colour identity and legality of your picks.")}
